1
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:52,156 --> 00:00:53,491
CANDIDATE 2, PARK HAE-KANG

3
00:00:55,743 --> 00:00:56,786
Cheers.

4
00:00:56,870 --> 00:01:00,540
Wait, Mr. Park. This calls for a toast.

5
00:01:00,623 --> 00:01:02,292
A toast? We don't do stuff like that.

6
00:01:02,375 --> 00:01:04,878
Then can I say something instead?

7
00:01:08,506 --> 00:01:09,340
Fine.

8
00:01:09,924 --> 00:01:11,301
That's great.

9
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,557
Everyone, you've all seen headlines like,

10
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:20,268
"Apartment complexes,
a hotbed of corruption!"

11
00:01:21,811 --> 00:01:24,981
Not writing up contracts properly,

12
00:01:25,064 --> 00:01:28,401
handing no-bid contracts
to favored companies,

13
00:01:28,484 --> 00:01:32,280
inflating construction costs,
embezzling maintenance funds…

14
00:01:32,363 --> 00:01:34,866
I don't want to see you guys on the news.

15
00:01:34,949 --> 00:01:38,745
So please,
don't get involved in such corruption.

16
00:01:38,828 --> 00:01:40,705
-I hope you finish your term
-This is boring.

17
00:01:40,788 --> 00:01:42,707
without any trouble, Mr. Park.

18
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:44,709
All right, then. Cheers!

19
00:01:44,792 --> 00:01:46,586
Cheers!

20
00:01:48,296 --> 00:01:49,839
Why the long faces?

21
00:01:50,423 --> 00:01:54,219
You made an intermittent family
and got the position you wanted so badly.

22
00:01:54,302 --> 00:01:55,595
Since it's come to this,

23
00:01:55,678 --> 00:01:59,390
I just wanted to encourage you,
as your fake wife, to do your best.

24
00:01:59,474 --> 00:02:00,892
Come on. Cheers!

25
00:02:00,975 --> 00:02:04,103
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

26
00:02:10,276 --> 00:02:11,444
How refreshing.

27
00:02:11,527 --> 00:02:13,196
Out of everything I've ever done,

28
00:02:13,279 --> 00:02:15,114
that was by far the hardest.

29
00:02:15,198 --> 00:02:18,159
The packages were piling up
like a mountain…

30
00:02:18,952 --> 00:02:21,287
What's with you? Why are you so drunk?

31
00:02:21,371 --> 00:02:22,622
He had a tough time.

32
00:02:22,705 --> 00:02:24,624
You have a chili flake
stuck in your teeth.

33
00:02:25,333 --> 00:02:26,918
I heard the good news.

34
00:02:28,586 --> 00:02:30,797
-Congratulations.
-You already heard?

35
00:02:34,384 --> 00:02:35,218
Blood?

36
00:02:46,729 --> 00:02:49,774
What's his deal? I'm sure that was blood.

37
00:02:53,319 --> 00:02:54,779
I'm almost there.

38
00:02:56,322 --> 00:02:57,615
Yong-man…

39
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:58,950
Just focus

40
00:03:00,368 --> 00:03:02,203
on saving Yong-man for now.

41
00:03:03,413 --> 00:03:08,334
THE APARTMENT JOB

42
00:03:15,758 --> 00:03:18,302
Right. That's nonsense.

43
00:03:19,679 --> 00:03:23,349
My elbow's been acting up.
I can't hit the ball well.

44
00:03:24,225 --> 00:03:25,351
-Are you okay?
-Goodness.

45
00:03:28,438 --> 00:03:30,440
Don't feel too upset about this, Mr. Lee.

46
00:03:31,149 --> 00:03:34,610
Right now, you're not in a position
to sit at the same table as us.

47
00:03:34,694 --> 00:03:36,320
It's just a tiny bump in the road.

48
00:03:36,404 --> 00:03:38,656
Mr. Lee wouldn't stumble
over something so small.

49
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:39,824
That'd be embarrassing.

50
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:42,994
This is so absurd, it's almost comical.

51
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:46,914
In any case, it's no big deal,
so don't worry about it.

52
00:03:46,998 --> 00:03:49,792
Eat up. You look so worn out.

53
00:03:50,668 --> 00:03:51,502
Yes, sir.

54
00:03:52,086 --> 00:03:53,546
Should we have gotten him beef?

55
00:03:54,422 --> 00:03:56,674
For workers, pork is still best.

56
00:03:58,259 --> 00:04:02,764
Even with a simple home renovation,
you run into all sorts of issues.

57
00:04:02,847 --> 00:04:05,141
But we're developing an entire city.

58
00:04:05,767 --> 00:04:06,726
You know,

59
00:04:06,809 --> 00:04:09,562
I just don't like Oman New Town
getting mentioned like this.

60
00:04:10,229 --> 00:04:12,815
I don't want this small spark

61
00:04:12,899 --> 00:04:16,444
turning into some huge corruption scandal
like in the movies.

62
00:04:16,527 --> 00:04:20,907
I want this wrapped up cleanly
without all that nonsense.

63
00:04:21,491 --> 00:04:25,244
Wrapping things up cleanly
is my specialty, you know.

64
00:04:48,976 --> 00:04:54,399
LEOPARD OF KILIMANJARO

65
00:05:02,907 --> 00:05:05,451
Have you ever seen a hyena
Roaming the foothills

66
00:05:05,535 --> 00:05:07,703
In search of prey?

67
00:05:07,787 --> 00:05:11,040
Hyenas roam the foothills
Only searching for carrion

68
00:05:11,874 --> 00:05:14,460
I want to be a leopard, not a hyena

69
00:05:16,879 --> 00:05:18,589
-He's inside, right?
-Yes, he is.

70
00:05:19,173 --> 00:05:20,842
How is he right now?

71
00:05:20,925 --> 00:05:23,761
I wake up great, then I wake up small

72
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:27,515
Now, I'm resting
In a dark corner of the world

73
00:05:27,598 --> 00:05:33,604
I can't just come like the wind
And leave like morning dew

74
00:05:34,605 --> 00:05:38,776
I should leave my mark behind

75
00:05:41,654 --> 00:05:43,906
I was feeling a little frustrated,

76
00:05:44,949 --> 00:05:47,577
so I wanted to sing this song first.

77
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,662
-Mr. Yoo.
-Yes?

78
00:05:50,246 --> 00:05:53,666
Didn't you conduct a cultural heritage
survey before construction started?

79
00:05:53,749 --> 00:05:54,834
We did, but--

80
00:05:54,917 --> 00:05:56,961
They found a bowl!

81
00:05:57,044 --> 00:05:59,213
Something that shouldn't have been found!

82
00:06:06,345 --> 00:06:09,015
It's bad enough that I spent my own money
digging up my own land

83
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,768
and discovered something
that shouldn't have been there.

84
00:06:14,478 --> 00:06:16,772
-Mr. Choi.
-Yes?

85
00:06:17,356 --> 00:06:20,818
How much interest
will I have to pay on my bank loan

86
00:06:20,902 --> 00:06:22,528
while the construction is on hold?

87
00:06:23,529 --> 00:06:25,114
Well…

88
00:06:25,948 --> 00:06:28,034
It's a pretty big amount.

89
00:06:33,289 --> 00:06:35,458
It's been a while.
Put your heads in position.

90
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:37,543
Sir…

91
00:06:37,627 --> 00:06:38,836
Heads in position!

92
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,338
-Yes, sir!
-Move!

93
00:07:04,612 --> 00:07:10,159
Love is lonely
Because you bet your fate on it

94
00:07:10,993 --> 00:07:15,039
Lonely because you risk everything

95
00:07:16,499 --> 00:07:17,500
I'm lonely.

96
00:07:18,918 --> 00:07:21,212
I feel like I'm the only one doing my job.

97
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:25,841
Find a way
to resume construction immediately!

98
00:07:27,051 --> 00:07:30,263
I'm sorry, sir,
but unless the relics are fake,

99
00:07:30,346 --> 00:07:34,016
-there's no way to reverse this!
-Mr. Park!

100
00:07:34,642 --> 00:07:37,103
Please forgive me, sir!

101
00:07:42,191 --> 00:07:43,025
Fake?

102
00:07:46,571 --> 00:07:48,239
What? You did what?

103
00:07:48,322 --> 00:07:50,366
-A fake wife?
-Yes.

104
00:07:50,449 --> 00:07:52,451
It's just like another stand-in gig.

105
00:07:52,535 --> 00:07:55,413
I get that you need the money,
but have you lost your mind?

106
00:07:55,496 --> 00:07:56,664
You wanted to be a lawyer.

107
00:07:56,747 --> 00:07:59,709
I'm going to start studying again
once I get the remaining money.

108
00:07:59,792 --> 00:08:01,127
There are only a few days left.

109
00:08:01,210 --> 00:08:02,336
Does Ha-jeong know?

110
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:03,754
Of course not.

111
00:08:04,839 --> 00:08:06,465
She's in France right now.

112
00:08:06,549 --> 00:08:09,635
I sent her there
with the advance payment I got.

113
00:08:10,219 --> 00:08:13,723
Her dream is to be a patissier,
so I told her to go and experience stuff.

114
00:08:13,806 --> 00:08:15,182
But why is that guy going so far

115
00:08:15,266 --> 00:08:18,477
as to fake a family to become
a residents' association president?

116
00:08:18,561 --> 00:08:19,437
What?

117
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,105
Just think about it.

118
00:08:21,188 --> 00:08:24,442
Why would he pay you that much
just for that position?

119
00:08:25,818 --> 00:08:26,819
I know.

120
00:08:28,279 --> 00:08:32,074
My mom's acquaintance's
in-law's cousin's friend--

121
00:08:32,158 --> 00:08:34,994
Yeong-ju, that's practically a stranger.

122
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:38,497
Right. Anyway, that stranger
became an apartment president

123
00:08:38,581 --> 00:08:41,000
and pocketed a huge sum.

124
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:45,671
They even got a new car
and moved to a fancy place too.

125
00:08:45,755 --> 00:08:47,423
-Could he also be--
-Hey.

126
00:08:47,506 --> 00:08:49,425
Mr. Park isn't that kind of person.

127
00:08:50,134 --> 00:08:51,552
Why are you shouting at me?

128
00:08:52,094 --> 00:08:54,722
Then what kind of man is he, exactly?

129
00:08:56,098 --> 00:08:56,932
What?

130
00:08:58,768 --> 00:08:59,935
Well, he's…

131
00:09:16,243 --> 00:09:18,204
What is Park Hae-kang doing on my ceiling?

132
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:20,539
Let's just sleep.

133
00:09:29,215 --> 00:09:30,800
-I'm here!
-Hi.

134
00:09:30,883 --> 00:09:32,677
-I'm not late, am I?
-You are.

135
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:35,054
What? Is it someone's birthday?

136
00:09:35,137 --> 00:09:38,349
No, but it's the first day
of our boss's term as president.

137
00:09:38,432 --> 00:09:39,850
I put my skills to use

138
00:09:39,934 --> 00:09:43,062
to make a hearty meal
to keep our strength up.

139
00:09:43,938 --> 00:09:46,899
Mr. Park, you're drinking
espresso again without eating?

140
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:48,651
I'm fine.

141
00:09:48,734 --> 00:09:50,486
It's not fine with me.

142
00:09:50,569 --> 00:09:52,738
Your brothers prepared
a nice meal for you.

143
00:09:52,822 --> 00:09:54,657
You should at least join them.

144
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:56,117
It's okay.

145
00:09:58,077 --> 00:09:58,911
Hey.

146
00:10:02,623 --> 00:10:03,791
Come on.

147
00:10:05,292 --> 00:10:07,128
Why are you doing this to me?

148
00:10:07,211 --> 00:10:09,797
It's seaweed soup. It's hot.

149
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:10,715
All right.

150
00:10:11,924 --> 00:10:12,758
Here.

151
00:10:12,842 --> 00:10:14,885
Should I feed it to you? Here.

152
00:10:15,511 --> 00:10:16,929
I'll eat it myself.

153
00:10:32,903 --> 00:10:34,447
This is good.

154
00:10:34,530 --> 00:10:36,240
You did great.

155
00:10:37,032 --> 00:10:38,784
You finally seem like an ordinary human.

156
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,541
Is that shaved ice?

157
00:10:47,209 --> 00:10:48,377
I'll give you more.

158
00:10:49,462 --> 00:10:50,296
Why are you crying?

159
00:10:51,005 --> 00:10:53,632
This is the first time
you've tried my cooking.

160
00:11:03,392 --> 00:11:04,643
So…

161
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:06,729
Dad.

162
00:11:06,812 --> 00:11:07,938
-Yes?
-Yes?

163
00:11:08,022 --> 00:11:09,064
Which dad?

164
00:11:09,648 --> 00:11:10,649
-Me?
-Me?

165
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:11,734
What is it?

166
00:11:14,236 --> 00:11:15,571
Do you have something to say?

167
00:11:18,824 --> 00:11:19,825
Mom.

168
00:11:22,369 --> 00:11:25,289
Ms. Kang, Gyeong-buk's calling you.

169
00:11:26,874 --> 00:11:29,293
I'm still not used to being called "Mom."
What is it?

170
00:11:33,088 --> 00:11:34,173
It's nothing.

171
00:11:38,385 --> 00:11:40,221
-I'm getting ready for work.
-Yes, sir.

172
00:11:40,304 --> 00:11:41,388
Yes, sir.

173
00:11:45,726 --> 00:11:47,478
It looks like
they're from every household.

174
00:11:47,561 --> 00:11:51,106
Seems like everyone was desperate
for a change in leadership.

175
00:11:51,190 --> 00:11:52,191
Sang-tae.

176
00:11:52,274 --> 00:11:54,360
-Yes?
-Watch your mouth.

177
00:11:54,443 --> 00:11:56,904
Someone could hear you. Be careful.

178
00:11:56,987 --> 00:11:58,364
But we're the only ones here.

179
00:11:59,657 --> 00:12:02,159
-Sorry.
-You should all lie low.

180
00:12:02,243 --> 00:12:05,412
A change in leadership
always brings a bloodbath.

181
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:08,499
I wouldn't go that far…

182
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:16,715
You're all so clueless.

183
00:12:19,385 --> 00:12:20,386
The blood…

184
00:12:22,388 --> 00:12:23,430
What are you waiting for?

185
00:12:23,514 --> 00:12:26,350
We should get ready
to welcome the new president.

186
00:12:26,934 --> 00:12:27,935
Let's…

187
00:12:28,644 --> 00:12:29,812
do a good job.

188
00:12:35,234 --> 00:12:37,695
If you don't want that
to happen to you, okay?

189
00:12:38,612 --> 00:12:40,030
Here's a gift.

190
00:12:57,423 --> 00:13:00,092
The bloodbath has already begun.

191
00:13:01,677 --> 00:13:03,470
Is it cold now?

192
00:13:05,347 --> 00:13:06,473
It's nice and cold.

193
00:13:08,684 --> 00:13:10,436
-Hold up.
-You scared me.

194
00:13:11,353 --> 00:13:14,273
It's okay to drink by yourself,

195
00:13:15,065 --> 00:13:19,069
but don't gamble at the senior center.

196
00:13:21,739 --> 00:13:23,324
I won't.

197
00:13:23,907 --> 00:13:26,452
I don't even have the money for that.

198
00:13:26,535 --> 00:13:27,411
I can't.

199
00:13:27,494 --> 00:13:30,914
You're someone to gamble
even if you're broke.

200
00:13:31,707 --> 00:13:34,209
If the boss finds out, you're dead.

201
00:13:34,793 --> 00:13:35,794
All right.

202
00:13:36,962 --> 00:13:38,464
Dad.

203
00:13:38,547 --> 00:13:40,716
Let me talk to your grandpa for a second.

204
00:13:40,799 --> 00:13:42,301
Okay.

205
00:13:43,677 --> 00:13:46,221
Ms. Kang, aren't you getting ready?

206
00:13:46,305 --> 00:13:47,640
Getting ready for what?

207
00:13:48,349 --> 00:13:50,100
We have to go to the management office.

208
00:13:50,976 --> 00:13:54,063
What? Mr. Park's the president.
Why would we go there?

209
00:13:54,146 --> 00:13:57,191
It's his first day of work.
We should go and support him.

210
00:13:57,274 --> 00:13:59,568
And something might happen to him,

211
00:14:00,069 --> 00:14:02,321
so we should show him
that we have his back.

212
00:14:02,404 --> 00:14:05,282
Heading to work on his first day
with the support of his family…

213
00:14:05,366 --> 00:14:07,117
-Wouldn't it be a beautiful sight?
-Yeah.

214
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:09,203
What do you mean by "beautiful"?

215
00:14:09,286 --> 00:14:12,456
It would be weird for a grown man's
entire family to follow him to work.

216
00:14:12,539 --> 00:14:14,625
But it's nothing hard to do.
You're getting paid.

217
00:14:14,708 --> 00:14:16,794
You should at least
do some things that we ask.

218
00:14:16,877 --> 00:14:20,756
Employees also have the right
to refuse unreasonable or unfair demands.

219
00:14:20,839 --> 00:14:21,715
Unbelievable.

220
00:14:21,799 --> 00:14:23,342
Neglect of duty, dereliction of duty.

221
00:14:23,425 --> 00:14:25,803
That's what you're doing right now,
Ms. Kang Ha-ri.

222
00:14:25,886 --> 00:14:27,763
As you may have noticed,
he went to law school.

223
00:14:27,846 --> 00:14:29,598
-Gosh.
-She should know too.

224
00:14:30,265 --> 00:14:33,102
Hey. Dereliction of duty
applies only to public officials.

225
00:14:33,185 --> 00:14:35,437
I'm not working as a public official here.

226
00:14:35,521 --> 00:14:37,022
How can you not know that?

227
00:14:38,023 --> 00:14:41,151
As you may have noticed,
she also attended law school.

228
00:14:41,235 --> 00:14:42,861
They should know too.

229
00:14:44,029 --> 00:14:46,407
Well, you're not an employee,
to be precise.

230
00:14:46,490 --> 00:14:48,492
How can you not know that?

231
00:14:49,076 --> 00:14:50,953
Oh, right. You failed the bar exam.

232
00:14:52,705 --> 00:14:53,789
What did you just say?

233
00:14:54,748 --> 00:14:58,043
I'll support him in my own way,
so just know that.

234
00:15:20,274 --> 00:15:21,859
You look nice, Mr. Park.

235
00:15:22,568 --> 00:15:24,361
You've succeeded, thanks to me.

236
00:15:28,323 --> 00:15:29,742
Mr. Park!

237
00:15:31,076 --> 00:15:34,663
True Value State's residents' association
president, Park Hae-kang!

238
00:15:34,747 --> 00:15:36,999
Good luck today!

239
00:15:37,082 --> 00:15:39,460
You look so cool, Hae-kang!

240
00:15:48,886 --> 00:15:50,888
Ha-ri, bring in the laundry.

241
00:15:56,018 --> 00:15:58,645
I can't believe I just did that.

242
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:02,733
But did all of them know
that I failed the bar exam?

243
00:16:02,816 --> 00:16:04,109
Darn it!

244
00:16:07,821 --> 00:16:09,615
I'm almost there.

245
00:16:09,698 --> 00:16:12,409
With the president's seal,
the facility manager's seal,

246
00:16:12,493 --> 00:16:16,580
and the apartment complex bank book,
this will all be over.

247
00:16:17,748 --> 00:16:18,707
Let's go.

248
00:16:22,503 --> 00:16:23,837
Good morning!

249
00:16:24,963 --> 00:16:26,423
Hello.

250
00:16:26,507 --> 00:16:27,800
Everyone's here again.

251
00:16:27,883 --> 00:16:29,551
Welcome, President Park.

252
00:16:30,469 --> 00:16:32,304
Your family's here too.

253
00:16:32,805 --> 00:16:34,890
-You really are…
-Hello!

254
00:16:35,474 --> 00:16:36,809
a close-knit family.

255
00:16:37,851 --> 00:16:39,978
-Are you busy, Mr. Choi?
-Not at all.

256
00:16:40,062 --> 00:16:42,481
I was just stamping
some payroll paperwork.

257
00:16:44,483 --> 00:16:47,027
Come on, Sang-tae.
Give him the thing we prepared.

258
00:16:47,778 --> 00:16:50,405
-Congratulations, President Park.
-Thank you.

259
00:16:50,489 --> 00:16:53,075
-It looks great on you.
-Thank you.

260
00:17:00,415 --> 00:17:03,418
I hope you like your office.

261
00:17:03,502 --> 00:17:05,379
I love it, Mr. Choi.

262
00:17:09,716 --> 00:17:10,968
And here.

263
00:17:11,051 --> 00:17:13,554
There are some basic handover notes,

264
00:17:13,637 --> 00:17:17,349
along with the bank book
and your stamp too.

265
00:17:17,432 --> 00:17:20,018
I look forward to working with you, sir.

266
00:17:32,281 --> 00:17:34,992
The power of the president.

267
00:17:35,576 --> 00:17:36,618
Pardon?

268
00:17:40,873 --> 00:17:43,709
You're always so interesting.

269
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:46,003
I'll get going then.

270
00:17:46,086 --> 00:17:48,297
You have a meeting
with the contractors later,

271
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:49,256
so don't forget.

272
00:17:52,176 --> 00:17:53,427
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

273
00:17:54,344 --> 00:17:55,637
-You're all so close.
-Yes.

274
00:18:08,942 --> 00:18:11,153
-It's beautiful.
-It's shining.

275
00:18:11,737 --> 00:18:13,322
-You did it, Boss.
-You did it.

276
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:16,783
It's not over yet, so stay sharp.

277
00:18:16,867 --> 00:18:18,076
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

278
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,703
Let's start wrapping things up.

279
00:18:19,786 --> 00:18:21,872
Once we get the money
from the bank tomorrow morning,

280
00:18:21,955 --> 00:18:23,457
-we're leaving immediately.
-Yes, sir.

281
00:18:24,041 --> 00:18:24,875
It's a large amount.

282
00:18:25,542 --> 00:18:27,961
-Gyeong-nam, prepare a bag for the cash.
-Yes, sir.

283
00:18:28,045 --> 00:18:30,297
Big Guy, sell off everything in the home.

284
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,298
Yes, sir.

285
00:18:31,381 --> 00:18:33,675
-Je-gil, get the facility manager's stamp.
-Yes, sir.

286
00:18:34,343 --> 00:18:35,469
The manager…

287
00:18:36,386 --> 00:18:39,890
just threw his stamp to the side
on his desk earlier.

288
00:18:41,141 --> 00:18:43,268
-Leave it to me, sir.
-He's so careless.

289
00:18:44,186 --> 00:18:46,313
What about the Lizard and Ms. Kang?

290
00:18:47,231 --> 00:18:49,775
-You shouldn't enter.
-It's fine.

291
00:18:49,858 --> 00:18:51,193
It's authorized personnel only.

292
00:18:51,276 --> 00:18:55,405
I'm the one who made him the president.
What do we call that again?

293
00:18:55,906 --> 00:18:56,782
Kingmaker?

294
00:18:56,865 --> 00:18:59,409
Yes. I'm the kingmaker,
so of course, I'm authorized.

295
00:18:59,493 --> 00:19:01,370
Don't you agree, Mr. Park?

296
00:19:02,537 --> 00:19:04,081
It's fine. You can go.

297
00:19:08,335 --> 00:19:09,920
Mr. Park.

298
00:19:10,504 --> 00:19:13,382
This is a gift
for your new position. Here.

299
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:16,468
What is this?

300
00:19:17,052 --> 00:19:18,720
Unwrap it. Go on.

301
00:19:19,221 --> 00:19:23,433
Our club members all felt so grateful,

302
00:19:23,517 --> 00:19:26,311
so we pitched in to get this made for you.

303
00:19:27,479 --> 00:19:29,606
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

304
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:31,149
Wow, a phoenix…

305
00:19:31,692 --> 00:19:33,944
Not even the President
would have a plaque like that.

306
00:19:34,695 --> 00:19:38,240
The position makes the person.

307
00:19:38,323 --> 00:19:43,078
You need something cool
like this right here…

308
00:19:44,246 --> 00:19:46,873
to give your desk some presence.

309
00:19:49,001 --> 00:19:51,878
Congratulations.

310
00:19:51,962 --> 00:19:54,423
Congratulations.

311
00:19:54,506 --> 00:19:58,343
Come on, Mr. Park. Congratulations.

312
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,099
It's nice, isn't it?

313
00:20:04,182 --> 00:20:05,934
So…

314
00:20:06,018 --> 00:20:09,521
we have to find something to pick at.

315
00:20:09,604 --> 00:20:14,901
We have to paint
Park Hae-kang's election as illegal.

316
00:20:15,485 --> 00:20:19,865
Then what should we pick at,
and how should we play it?

317
00:20:19,948 --> 00:20:24,494
Maybe we can make an issue
of his candidate registration form.

318
00:20:24,578 --> 00:20:27,080
How about Park Hae-kang's photo size?

319
00:20:27,164 --> 00:20:30,083
He used a larger photo than yours.

320
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:31,251
What do you think?

321
00:20:31,335 --> 00:20:34,087
He did violate the rules, didn't he?

322
00:20:34,171 --> 00:20:35,547
We can't solve this problem

323
00:20:35,630 --> 00:20:38,216
by making an issue
of something so trivial.

324
00:20:40,177 --> 00:20:41,303
Not something like that.

325
00:20:41,386 --> 00:20:45,599
We need something
that can bring him down in one go.

326
00:20:45,682 --> 00:20:46,725
Something critical.

327
00:20:46,808 --> 00:20:50,854
Mr. Lee, you took a lot of kickbacks
from Hansong Equipment, didn't you?

328
00:20:51,688 --> 00:20:52,856
And Ms. Kim.

329
00:20:52,939 --> 00:20:56,860
I know you accepted a lot of money
from Director Park

330
00:20:56,943 --> 00:20:58,904
during the bidding
for the kindergarten contract.

331
00:20:58,987 --> 00:21:01,281
And Mr. Oh,

332
00:21:01,365 --> 00:21:04,242
you pulled some strings
to get your sibling hired

333
00:21:04,326 --> 00:21:05,911
at the landscaping company.

334
00:21:05,994 --> 00:21:08,497
I can easily come up
with a long list of stuff like this

335
00:21:09,081 --> 00:21:11,291
just by thinking for a second.

336
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:15,796
But you look much too relaxed right now.

337
00:21:17,631 --> 00:21:18,799
I really…

338
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:22,511
Listen.

339
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:27,682
If we can't get rid of Park Hae-kang,

340
00:21:27,766 --> 00:21:30,477
if we fail to drag him down
from that position,

341
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:33,063
we're all dead!

342
00:21:33,146 --> 00:21:34,898
We're all going down.

343
00:21:36,024 --> 00:21:37,109
Do you understand?

344
00:21:37,192 --> 00:21:39,736
Ever heard the saying,
"Power never lasts"?

345
00:21:40,362 --> 00:21:42,781
It means no one can stay in power forever.

346
00:21:44,282 --> 00:21:47,577
President Park, you really are smart.

347
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:51,748
They say power cannot last ten years.

348
00:21:51,832 --> 00:21:55,919
But foolish humans always grow corrupt,

349
00:21:56,420 --> 00:21:57,629
thinking it will last forever.

350
00:21:57,712 --> 00:22:01,633
That is why I'm offering to manage

351
00:22:01,716 --> 00:22:03,969
that kind of stuff for you.

352
00:22:04,052 --> 00:22:05,762
-What stuff?
-You know.

353
00:22:08,348 --> 00:22:10,392
Family risk.

354
00:22:11,101 --> 00:22:14,438
Politicians back then
all had family scandals.

355
00:22:14,521 --> 00:22:18,984
No matter how good a politician you are,
one family scandal can bring you down.

356
00:22:19,734 --> 00:22:21,153
Well, I guess so.

357
00:22:21,236 --> 00:22:23,447
But that has nothing to do with us.

358
00:22:23,530 --> 00:22:25,574
Of course, it does.

359
00:22:25,657 --> 00:22:30,287
Power and corruption
are practically inseparable.

360
00:22:30,370 --> 00:22:35,167
That is why I'm offering to become
your Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs

361
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:38,879
and manage such issues for you.

362
00:22:38,962 --> 00:22:40,672
-Senior Secretary?
-Senior Secretary?

363
00:22:42,174 --> 00:22:45,510
Yes. Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.
Isn't that nice?

364
00:22:45,594 --> 00:22:49,514
I just want to see you
for a long time, that's all.

365
00:22:49,598 --> 00:22:51,016
So let me do that for you.

366
00:22:51,099 --> 00:22:53,852
Okay? I'll be the Senior Secretary
for Civil Affairs.

367
00:22:56,730 --> 00:22:57,898
Are you ready, sir?

368
00:22:57,981 --> 00:23:01,693
-You're here too, Ms. Jang.
-Yes, Mr. Choi.

369
00:23:03,361 --> 00:23:04,196
President Park,

370
00:23:04,988 --> 00:23:05,864
are you ready?

371
00:23:10,202 --> 00:23:11,286
Let's go!

372
00:23:14,998 --> 00:23:16,666
Will it be okay to leave her be?

373
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:18,543
-This is bad.
-What's "Senior Secretary"?

374
00:23:18,627 --> 00:23:20,545
It's fine. We're leaving tomorrow.

375
00:23:20,629 --> 00:23:23,965
-You guys go and get ready.
-Where's my coat? Bring my coat!

376
00:23:24,049 --> 00:23:25,759
-Give me that.
-Boss.

377
00:23:27,177 --> 00:23:29,137
-I can…
-Coming!

378
00:23:33,433 --> 00:23:36,019
As you know, there are three floors

379
00:23:36,102 --> 00:23:39,731
with 121 shops in our apartment complex.

380
00:23:39,814 --> 00:23:41,149
This way, sir.

381
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:44,694
Gosh.

382
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:51,409
Congratulations on becoming
the residents' association president!

383
00:23:51,493 --> 00:23:53,370
-Congratulations!
-Congratulations!

384
00:23:56,623 --> 00:23:59,334
I'm True Value State's new president,
Park Hae-kang.

385
00:23:59,417 --> 00:24:00,543
Nice to meet you all.

386
00:24:00,627 --> 00:24:01,670
Applause!

387
00:24:03,922 --> 00:24:05,799
We look forward to working with you.

388
00:24:05,882 --> 00:24:09,177
This is our merchants' association
membership list.

389
00:24:10,595 --> 00:24:13,640
If you visit any of our shops
and tell us you're the president,

390
00:24:13,723 --> 00:24:15,267
everything will be on the house.

391
00:24:16,434 --> 00:24:17,727
On the house? Why?

392
00:24:18,728 --> 00:24:20,647
Because you're the president.

393
00:24:21,982 --> 00:24:23,566
That includes your family too.

394
00:24:26,987 --> 00:24:31,283
Our president doesn't accept
bribes of any kind.

395
00:24:34,035 --> 00:24:35,453
-Let's go.
-Right.

396
00:24:38,832 --> 00:24:40,375
Our president is here.

397
00:24:44,379 --> 00:24:47,716
Everyone,
as his Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs,

398
00:24:47,799 --> 00:24:49,926
let me make an important announcement.

399
00:24:50,552 --> 00:24:53,596
President Park will not accept
bribes of any kind.

400
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:56,891
Take back everything you brought.

401
00:24:58,977 --> 00:25:00,437
Take them back.

402
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:03,064
We look forward to working with you,
President Park!

403
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:09,112
Let's go, True Value!

404
00:25:18,455 --> 00:25:19,289
Sir.

405
00:25:19,956 --> 00:25:20,832
Here.

406
00:25:20,915 --> 00:25:22,083
For your hard work.

407
00:25:27,422 --> 00:25:28,423
What is this?

408
00:25:29,341 --> 00:25:30,842
Take that

409
00:25:30,925 --> 00:25:35,138
and announce that all the relics
found here were fabricated.

410
00:25:36,181 --> 00:25:39,142
Relics like this
can't have been discovered here.

411
00:25:40,935 --> 00:25:42,020
You really…

412
00:25:43,063 --> 00:25:44,564
are quick-witted.

413
00:25:44,647 --> 00:25:46,816
You understood right away.

414
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:49,986
Make an announcement
with what you just said.

415
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:55,408
No, I'm serious. It's almost impossible
for such relics to be found here.

416
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,119
What?

417
00:26:01,956 --> 00:26:04,793
The soil on the relics doesn't match,

418
00:26:04,876 --> 00:26:07,379
and they're all from different periods.

419
00:26:07,462 --> 00:26:10,965
They can't have been found like this
unless someone planted them here.

420
00:26:12,258 --> 00:26:14,928
So someone planted them on purpose?

421
00:26:18,890 --> 00:26:20,975
If I catch whoever did this,

422
00:26:21,851 --> 00:26:23,311
I'm going to kill them.

423
00:26:34,197 --> 00:26:36,282
-Hello?
-Hey, cop.

424
00:26:36,866 --> 00:26:38,785
You got the call from Mr. Song, right?

425
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:42,163
I need some help from you.

426
00:27:02,392 --> 00:27:03,852
I LOVE YOU, RU-I

427
00:27:30,211 --> 00:27:31,254
Gyeong-buk.

428
00:27:36,217 --> 00:27:38,887
Ha-ri, what are you doing here?

429
00:27:39,512 --> 00:27:41,264
I just made a parking account

430
00:27:41,347 --> 00:27:43,975
with the benefits of a checking account
and a savings account.

431
00:27:44,058 --> 00:27:47,353
Right. You can make deposits
and withdrawals with daily interest.

432
00:27:47,437 --> 00:27:49,397
-I heard about it.
-Yeah, that one.

433
00:27:50,356 --> 00:27:53,985
A savings plan felt like too much,
so this was perfect for me.

434
00:27:54,068 --> 00:27:56,112
I should make one too.
I really wanted this plushie.

435
00:27:56,196 --> 00:27:58,490
Hey. Just take it.

436
00:28:00,116 --> 00:28:01,367
You can make one online too.

437
00:28:01,451 --> 00:28:02,827
-Really?
-Look.

438
00:28:09,250 --> 00:28:10,168
Hello?

439
00:28:10,251 --> 00:28:13,963
This is True Value Kindergarten.
Is this Gyeong-buk's mom?

440
00:28:14,506 --> 00:28:16,424
You've got the wrong number.

441
00:28:16,508 --> 00:28:18,009
Wait! Hello?

442
00:28:18,092 --> 00:28:20,136
Yes, I'm Gyeong-buk's mom.

443
00:28:20,845 --> 00:28:23,348
You're his kindergarten teacher.

444
00:28:23,973 --> 00:28:25,183
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

445
00:28:25,266 --> 00:28:29,771
You must be exhausted from all that work,
President Park.

446
00:28:29,854 --> 00:28:32,023
Here, drink this.

447
00:28:32,607 --> 00:28:35,193
Here. Cheers.

448
00:28:38,613 --> 00:28:40,240
Mr. Park, there's an emergency…

449
00:28:41,533 --> 00:28:42,700
Gosh.

450
00:28:42,784 --> 00:28:48,540
Ma'am, you should be careful
of how you address him in public.

451
00:28:48,623 --> 00:28:51,251
Did you just call him "Mr. Park"?

452
00:28:51,751 --> 00:28:52,752
You're married, you know.

453
00:28:56,422 --> 00:28:58,967
-Honey.
-Yes, dear?

454
00:28:59,717 --> 00:29:01,594
Gyeong-buk's having a sports day today.

455
00:29:01,678 --> 00:29:04,806
All the other parents are playing games,
but we're the only ones absent.

456
00:29:06,266 --> 00:29:07,934
Do you have something to say?

457
00:29:10,603 --> 00:29:13,690
That's what he was trying to say
this morning. Let's go.

458
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:16,526
Goodness. What are you doing?

459
00:29:16,609 --> 00:29:19,404
President Park,
you have a huge pile of work to do.

460
00:29:19,487 --> 00:29:21,322
You can't go.

461
00:29:21,406 --> 00:29:24,784
Ma'am, mothers should
take care of such matters.

462
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:28,121
Why should I go alone?
He has a father too.

463
00:29:28,204 --> 00:29:33,626
For a man to achieve great things,
his family needs to make some sacrifices.

464
00:29:34,335 --> 00:29:35,169
Ms. Jang.

465
00:29:36,045 --> 00:29:38,965
Would events held by the kindergarten
mostly be attended

466
00:29:39,048 --> 00:29:40,967
-by parents of True Value?
-Of course.

467
00:29:41,050 --> 00:29:43,052
Then I'd say this is the perfect chance

468
00:29:43,136 --> 00:29:46,055
to solidify my position as the president

469
00:29:46,139 --> 00:29:47,891
and build the image of a loving father.

470
00:29:47,974 --> 00:29:49,726
What do you think, Ms. Jang?

471
00:29:53,187 --> 00:29:56,524
Then I'll clear out your entire afternoon.

472
00:30:08,536 --> 00:30:10,163
Wait for me!

473
00:30:10,246 --> 00:30:12,749
Riding the waves with Mom and Dad!

474
00:30:12,832 --> 00:30:13,791
Ready, go!

475
00:30:14,500 --> 00:30:17,045
Go, Team Pink! Go, Team Blue!

476
00:30:17,128 --> 00:30:19,088
Go, Team Pink!

477
00:30:19,172 --> 00:30:21,174
Go! Look at Team Pink!

478
00:30:21,257 --> 00:30:22,550
Team Pink wins!

479
00:30:22,634 --> 00:30:25,303
Team Pink won! Your team won, Gyeong-buk!

480
00:30:26,971 --> 00:30:29,432
-Let's do it together next.
-No.

481
00:30:29,515 --> 00:30:31,643
Why? Come on. Let's do it together.

482
00:30:43,112 --> 00:30:48,576
Everyone, True Value's
President Park Hae-kang is here.

483
00:30:49,077 --> 00:30:50,703
He's Gyeong-buk's father.

484
00:30:51,955 --> 00:30:53,498
I'm Park Hae-kang.

485
00:30:53,581 --> 00:30:54,832
Gyeong-buk!

486
00:30:57,835 --> 00:31:00,713
-They do kind of look alike.
-So he's his son.

487
00:31:02,674 --> 00:31:03,758
How did you know?

488
00:31:03,841 --> 00:31:05,218
I know everything.

489
00:31:10,515 --> 00:31:13,351
Gyeong-buk, why didn't you tell us
today was Sports Day?

490
00:31:13,434 --> 00:31:15,061
This isn't some huge secret.

491
00:31:15,937 --> 00:31:18,898
Because we're not a real family.

492
00:31:22,026 --> 00:31:25,238
I'll show you that I can do even better
since I'm not real.

493
00:31:26,614 --> 00:31:27,615
They're all dead.

494
00:31:27,699 --> 00:31:30,493
I'm going to defeat
all the mothers here today!

495
00:31:30,576 --> 00:31:31,577
Let's win!

496
00:31:35,164 --> 00:31:37,625
EXPANDABLE LUGGAGE BAGS

497
00:31:38,292 --> 00:31:40,962
-Sir.
-What are you looking for?

498
00:31:41,546 --> 00:31:44,674
Are these all the bags you have?
They're smaller than I thought.

499
00:31:45,258 --> 00:31:46,509
Small?

500
00:31:47,635 --> 00:31:49,637
You have no idea.

501
00:31:50,138 --> 00:31:53,141
They can expand like magic.

502
00:31:53,224 --> 00:31:54,767
You can fit ten billion in cash.

503
00:31:57,020 --> 00:31:59,355
Then I'll need at least two.

504
00:31:59,439 --> 00:32:01,482
What? You have 20 billion?

505
00:32:02,734 --> 00:32:05,361
I wish. How much is it?

506
00:32:05,945 --> 00:32:09,157
-Let's go eat, everyone.
-Yes, sir.

507
00:32:20,585 --> 00:32:23,713
Geez. Why isn't this working?
This is driving me crazy.

508
00:32:24,964 --> 00:32:27,550
-Hello.
-You're the president's brother.

509
00:32:27,633 --> 00:32:29,844
He's not here right now, though.
Can I help you?

510
00:32:29,927 --> 00:32:32,680
Oh, he's not here.
I thought we could have lunch…

511
00:32:33,514 --> 00:32:34,640
Is that broken?

512
00:32:37,185 --> 00:32:38,644
Thank you!

513
00:32:38,728 --> 00:32:41,773
I would've gotten scolded again
if it weren't for you.

514
00:32:41,856 --> 00:32:43,191
Is this for a meeting?

515
00:32:43,274 --> 00:32:44,984
It's our business plan for this year.

516
00:32:45,902 --> 00:32:49,072
The president changed,
so we need a new one.

517
00:32:50,073 --> 00:32:52,658
I didn't mean I'm unhappy
that the president changed.

518
00:32:52,742 --> 00:32:54,202
Should I put this on his desk?

519
00:32:54,285 --> 00:32:56,704
You're really kind, unlike how you look.

520
00:33:07,423 --> 00:33:10,676
Is there anything else I can help with?
You can ask me anything.

521
00:33:13,846 --> 00:33:14,680
Excuse me.

522
00:33:15,807 --> 00:33:18,392
Are you Mr. Used Goods Fairy?

523
00:33:20,812 --> 00:33:22,396
-You're Mr. No Discount?
-Yes.

524
00:33:23,106 --> 00:33:24,315
The rice cooker…

525
00:33:24,398 --> 00:33:25,733
-The rice cooker.
-Yes.

526
00:33:28,361 --> 00:33:29,403
-Here.
-Right.

527
00:33:29,487 --> 00:33:30,613
-It works well.
-Okay.

528
00:33:30,696 --> 00:33:32,281
-No refunds or exchanges.
-Okay.

529
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:35,034
Here.

530
00:33:35,743 --> 00:33:37,036
Thank you for the discount,

531
00:33:37,620 --> 00:33:38,955
Mr. Used Goods Fairy.

532
00:33:41,207 --> 00:33:42,291
Please write a good review.

533
00:33:52,468 --> 00:33:55,179
A round of applause
for Gyeong-buk's father's kick!

534
00:34:46,939 --> 00:34:48,274
Go!

535
00:34:51,235 --> 00:34:53,613
Go, Mom! Go!

536
00:35:00,620 --> 00:35:01,746
It's neck and neck!

537
00:35:04,415 --> 00:35:06,667
Gyeong-buk's mother is in first place!

538
00:35:06,751 --> 00:35:09,003
Gyeong-buk's mother wins!

539
00:35:15,051 --> 00:35:16,469
With more energy!

540
00:35:30,316 --> 00:35:32,443
Don't hesitate! Dance with more energy!

541
00:35:33,277 --> 00:35:34,403
Today's highlight.

542
00:35:34,487 --> 00:35:38,783
This game will be a four-legged race
to demonstrate family unity.

543
00:35:38,866 --> 00:35:43,162
Children from the winning teams
will get to choose their own reward.

544
00:35:43,246 --> 00:35:46,666
You'll start at the sound of the whistle.

545
00:35:46,749 --> 00:35:47,875
Ready…

546
00:35:57,301 --> 00:36:00,805
Go!

547
00:36:00,888 --> 00:36:02,640
-Go!
-Go!

548
00:36:02,723 --> 00:36:03,849
Park Hae-kang!

549
00:36:20,950 --> 00:36:21,951
Oh my gosh.

550
00:36:28,916 --> 00:36:31,627
Ms. Kang, get up.

551
00:36:32,628 --> 00:36:34,338
Help me.

552
00:36:35,423 --> 00:36:36,424
Sorry, Gyeong-buk.

553
00:36:36,507 --> 00:36:37,842
Are you okay?

554
00:36:37,925 --> 00:36:39,343
Go!

555
00:36:40,344 --> 00:36:42,096
President Park!

556
00:36:42,179 --> 00:36:44,307
Beef! Ginseng!

557
00:36:45,308 --> 00:36:47,643
We can't give up. Let's go!

558
00:36:47,727 --> 00:36:48,728
Let's go.

559
00:36:57,945 --> 00:36:59,613
-There you go!
-We can do it!

560
00:37:13,586 --> 00:37:16,297
The team in first place
chose the ginseng set.

561
00:37:16,380 --> 00:37:18,466
What will you choose, Gyeong-buk?

562
00:37:20,134 --> 00:37:20,968
Beef.

563
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:23,804
Choose the beef.

564
00:37:24,847 --> 00:37:25,681
The beef.

565
00:37:28,434 --> 00:37:30,061
The hair roller set.

566
00:37:30,144 --> 00:37:31,854
I want this one.

567
00:37:31,937 --> 00:37:32,813
Gyeong-buk.

568
00:37:33,314 --> 00:37:34,774
Why would you…

569
00:37:34,857 --> 00:37:37,234
There are lots of other great gifts.
Why that one?

570
00:37:37,318 --> 00:37:41,822
I saw on TV that other moms all have this,

571
00:37:41,906 --> 00:37:43,991
but my mom, Kang Ha-ri,
doesn't seem to have one.

572
00:37:46,869 --> 00:37:48,537
-What a good son.
-So admirable.

573
00:37:48,621 --> 00:37:49,997
Sons are the best.

574
00:37:50,081 --> 00:37:52,750
Goodness. What a good son.

575
00:37:55,836 --> 00:37:57,588
You're such a great son.

576
00:37:57,671 --> 00:38:00,174
You were worried about my hair. Let's see.

577
00:38:00,257 --> 00:38:02,301
There are different kinds of hair rollers.

578
00:38:02,385 --> 00:38:04,553
This is much better than beef.

579
00:38:05,137 --> 00:38:06,138
Thank you, Gyeong-buk.

580
00:38:06,222 --> 00:38:10,559
Our Gyeong-buk
is so considerate, isn't he?

581
00:38:10,643 --> 00:38:13,813
Give our kind Gyeong-buk
a round of applause!

582
00:38:14,397 --> 00:38:16,023
Yes, let's give a round of applause.

583
00:38:16,690 --> 00:38:18,359
I'm so happy.

584
00:38:23,114 --> 00:38:25,282
He chose hair rollers
over beef and ginseng.

585
00:38:25,366 --> 00:38:28,244
Does Gyeong-buk like me that much?

586
00:38:28,911 --> 00:38:30,830
How do I look? Pretty?

587
00:38:39,213 --> 00:38:40,631
What kind of reaction is that?

588
00:38:42,716 --> 00:38:45,803
I'll give my bangs some volume
before coming to work tomorrow.

589
00:38:45,886 --> 00:38:47,763
Boss, everything's done.

590
00:38:49,223 --> 00:38:50,391
Ms. Kang.

591
00:38:52,059 --> 00:38:53,060
Yes?

592
00:38:59,191 --> 00:39:00,276
Ms. Kang.

593
00:39:01,152 --> 00:39:03,487
You don't have to come to work anymore.

594
00:39:04,738 --> 00:39:07,867
What? What do you mean?

595
00:39:07,950 --> 00:39:09,618
It hasn't been two weeks yet.

596
00:39:09,702 --> 00:39:11,287
You don't have to fill the two weeks.

597
00:39:11,370 --> 00:39:14,248
I'll transfer the money to you by today.

598
00:39:14,331 --> 00:39:16,750
Great work. You can go now.

599
00:39:18,586 --> 00:39:20,796
You're just sending me off right now?

600
00:39:21,589 --> 00:39:24,967
-My bag is still there--
-I'll have your things delivered to you.

601
00:39:30,222 --> 00:39:31,348
Take a cab home.

602
00:39:34,727 --> 00:39:36,937
Goodbye then.

603
00:39:44,487 --> 00:39:45,488
What?

604
00:40:03,756 --> 00:40:06,675
Isn't that ridiculous?

605
00:40:07,593 --> 00:40:08,677
How could he do this?

606
00:40:08,761 --> 00:40:13,265
How can he just treat me like this

607
00:40:13,349 --> 00:40:15,809
after all the time we spent together?

608
00:40:15,893 --> 00:40:18,395
Was that all just a lie?

609
00:40:18,479 --> 00:40:19,480
Yeah.

610
00:40:19,563 --> 00:40:21,857
Of course it was.
It was a stand-in service.

611
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:24,318
Still…

612
00:40:24,401 --> 00:40:27,404
How could he just send me away
so coldly like that?

613
00:40:27,488 --> 00:40:28,572
Forget it.

614
00:40:28,656 --> 00:40:30,282
You got the rest of the payment.

615
00:40:30,366 --> 00:40:32,284
You should focus on your studies now.

616
00:40:33,327 --> 00:40:35,246
I will, but…

617
00:40:35,955 --> 00:40:37,790
I just feel so upset.

618
00:41:10,489 --> 00:41:12,157
-Boss.
-Yes?

619
00:41:13,117 --> 00:41:14,868
-Here.
-Right.

620
00:41:14,952 --> 00:41:16,287
Good job.

621
00:41:16,787 --> 00:41:18,455
You all did great.

622
00:41:18,539 --> 00:41:21,667
We just have to drop by the bank
tomorrow morning and leave.

623
00:41:22,876 --> 00:41:23,961
What about Gyeong-nam?

624
00:41:24,044 --> 00:41:25,504
He went to take Gyeong-buk back.

625
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:28,507
But sir, what about Ms. Kang?

626
00:41:30,426 --> 00:41:31,802
-It's done.
-What?

627
00:41:32,595 --> 00:41:34,346
You don't need to worry about it.

628
00:41:35,055 --> 00:41:37,308
We didn't even get to say goodbye to her.

629
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:53,073
It's really stretchy.

630
00:41:53,157 --> 00:41:54,408
Looks yummy.

631
00:41:54,491 --> 00:41:55,868
-Eat up.
-Okay.

632
00:41:58,579 --> 00:41:59,580
It's good.

633
00:41:59,663 --> 00:42:01,540
-Is it? Eat as much as you want.
-Yes.

634
00:42:06,253 --> 00:42:07,129
Gyeong-buk.

635
00:42:09,256 --> 00:42:12,259
It was tough living in Seoul, wasn't it?

636
00:42:12,843 --> 00:42:13,927
What do you mean?

637
00:42:14,011 --> 00:42:18,182
I mean, there were lots of people at home.
Even a weird grandpa.

638
00:42:18,265 --> 00:42:21,226
You suddenly had a mom and several uncles.

639
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:22,936
And I made you lie

640
00:42:23,020 --> 00:42:26,315
and call Uncle Hae-kang your dad.

641
00:42:27,107 --> 00:42:28,192
No.

642
00:42:28,275 --> 00:42:31,070
I was happy to have Mom, my uncles,

643
00:42:31,654 --> 00:42:33,489
and Grandpa there.

644
00:42:34,698 --> 00:42:36,158
I want to do it again.

645
00:42:36,742 --> 00:42:38,744
I think I like having a family, Dad.

646
00:42:44,249 --> 00:42:47,002
We'll be a family again next time.

647
00:42:47,086 --> 00:42:49,088
Okay. Promise?

648
00:42:59,807 --> 00:43:01,684
I saw it. There's no need to hide it.

649
00:43:02,643 --> 00:43:05,229
You really should quit gambling now, sir.

650
00:43:07,690 --> 00:43:08,691
Mr. Park.

651
00:43:09,942 --> 00:43:11,235
Did you just…

652
00:43:12,111 --> 00:43:13,612
speak politely to me?

653
00:43:14,947 --> 00:43:17,825
You're not young anymore.
Are you going to keep living like this?

654
00:43:18,784 --> 00:43:21,370
You're scaring me, Mr. Park.

655
00:43:24,039 --> 00:43:26,041
Did I do something wrong again?

656
00:43:26,750 --> 00:43:29,545
Don't kill me. You said you'd let me live.

657
00:43:30,295 --> 00:43:32,423
It's not that. Just sit comfortably.

658
00:43:33,006 --> 00:43:34,007
Come on.

659
00:43:39,346 --> 00:43:40,597
You did a great job.

660
00:43:41,348 --> 00:43:44,601
I'll cancel the debt you owe
to our gambling den.

661
00:43:45,644 --> 00:43:46,645
Mr. Park.

662
00:43:48,689 --> 00:43:49,773
So you got everything.

663
00:43:52,901 --> 00:43:54,194
Is tomorrow the big day?

664
00:43:55,070 --> 00:43:58,031
Once we drop by the bank tomorrow
and get the money,

665
00:43:58,115 --> 00:43:59,658
I'll give you a portion.

666
00:44:01,618 --> 00:44:03,620
No, Mr. Park.

667
00:44:04,163 --> 00:44:07,207
It's fine. I'm really fine.

668
00:44:08,333 --> 00:44:11,795
I'm already grateful
that you let me stay and hide here.

669
00:44:11,879 --> 00:44:12,838
Are you sure?

670
00:44:12,921 --> 00:44:15,716
Yes. I'm really okay.

671
00:44:16,383 --> 00:44:17,760
Live a decent life now.

672
00:44:20,012 --> 00:44:20,846
I will.

673
00:44:24,141 --> 00:44:26,393
You know I have contacts
everywhere, right?

674
00:44:27,478 --> 00:44:31,565
If I ever hear that you're gambling again,
then I'll really cut off your hands.

675
00:44:34,234 --> 00:44:35,235
Get some sleep.

676
00:44:54,546 --> 00:44:55,756
He's…

677
00:44:57,132 --> 00:44:58,967
really thoughtful.

678
00:45:04,264 --> 00:45:06,308
How handsome.

679
00:45:10,896 --> 00:45:14,233
We'll hit the bank in the morning,
get the money, send it to Mr. Son,

680
00:45:14,316 --> 00:45:15,484
then leave Seoul.

681
00:45:15,567 --> 00:45:17,986
I found an island
where we can lie low for a while.

682
00:45:18,070 --> 00:45:20,280
-And the Lizard?
-I told him to go to our car.

683
00:45:22,491 --> 00:45:25,202
Let's start over
after we get Yong-man back.

684
00:45:25,285 --> 00:45:26,537
-Yes, Boss.
-Yes, Boss.

685
00:45:27,663 --> 00:45:28,747
Let's go.

686
00:46:03,865 --> 00:46:05,659
How may I help you?

687
00:46:05,742 --> 00:46:07,869
I'd like to withdraw
the entire amount in cash.

688
00:46:11,290 --> 00:46:13,584
-The entire amount?
-Yes.

689
00:46:16,545 --> 00:46:17,796
Do you live in an apartment?

690
00:46:18,964 --> 00:46:20,632
-Yes.
-Then you'd know.

691
00:46:21,216 --> 00:46:25,220
We have some major construction coming up.
I'm the residents' association president.

692
00:46:25,804 --> 00:46:28,640
As you know,
it costs a fortune to replace an elevator.

693
00:46:31,268 --> 00:46:33,353
-Should I give you this bag?
-No, it's fine.

694
00:46:33,437 --> 00:46:34,980
-Just a moment.
-All right.

695
00:46:52,831 --> 00:46:53,832
What is this?

696
00:46:53,915 --> 00:46:56,209
You wanted the entire amount.

697
00:46:56,293 --> 00:46:59,296
It's 2,530 won.

698
00:47:15,479 --> 00:47:16,688
I want to withdraw everything.

699
00:47:16,772 --> 00:47:19,608
Your balance is 7,280 won.

700
00:47:20,984 --> 00:47:22,736
He's taking a long time.

701
00:47:22,819 --> 00:47:24,321
Is it too heavy to carry on his own?

702
00:47:24,404 --> 00:47:26,114
Here's your 7,650 won.

703
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:31,953
Here's your full balance. 4,910 won.

704
00:47:32,037 --> 00:47:33,205
Of course, it's heavy.

705
00:47:33,288 --> 00:47:34,539
Should we have gone with him?

706
00:47:39,670 --> 00:47:42,923
The money is in different banks,
so obviously, it'll take a while.

707
00:47:44,508 --> 00:47:46,385
Here's your total of 9,220 won.

708
00:47:49,846 --> 00:47:50,847
MIRAE BANK

709
00:47:58,438 --> 00:47:59,606
This can't be true.

710
00:47:59,690 --> 00:48:01,983
The long-term repair reserve fund?

711
00:48:02,067 --> 00:48:04,277
There's 17,857,420,000 won.

712
00:48:04,361 --> 00:48:06,738
They said it was there. Where is it?

713
00:48:06,822 --> 00:48:08,949
I went through so much for that money.

714
00:48:09,032 --> 00:48:13,078
I'm Candidate 3 for District 4,
Park Hae-kang!

715
00:48:13,161 --> 00:48:14,413
I'll take care of this problem!

716
00:48:14,496 --> 00:48:15,330
So dig.

717
00:48:16,540 --> 00:48:17,833
-Park Hae-kang!
-Park Hae-kang!

718
00:48:17,916 --> 00:48:20,335
Move Exit 3 to True Value!

719
00:48:21,712 --> 00:48:23,004
I worked so hard for this.

720
00:48:26,216 --> 00:48:28,719
The 17,857,420,000 won…

721
00:48:29,469 --> 00:48:30,804
Where is my money?

722
00:48:33,473 --> 00:48:36,435
My 17,857,420,000 won!

723
00:48:36,518 --> 00:48:38,186
Where is it?

724
00:48:42,149 --> 00:48:44,776
Mr. Park! Please let me out!

725
00:48:44,860 --> 00:48:46,820
I'm going to suffocate to death!

726
00:48:46,903 --> 00:48:48,488
Please!

727
00:48:48,572 --> 00:48:49,614
Please…

728
00:48:54,911 --> 00:48:56,538
I'm claustrophobic.

729
00:48:58,874 --> 00:49:00,667
Why are we on the roof again?

730
00:49:00,751 --> 00:49:03,628
I'm scared of heights too!

731
00:49:05,714 --> 00:49:07,257
The money isn't there!

732
00:49:07,841 --> 00:49:12,637
The 17,857,420,000 won.
It's not there. Why?

733
00:49:12,721 --> 00:49:15,140
I'm frustrated too.

734
00:49:15,223 --> 00:49:19,060
We all heard it over the phone that day.
She said they had 17.8 billion.

735
00:49:19,144 --> 00:49:21,646
You should be looking
for the one who took it

736
00:49:21,730 --> 00:49:24,191
instead of taking it out on me.

737
00:49:24,274 --> 00:49:26,693
Fine. Then how do we find this person?

738
00:49:26,777 --> 00:49:28,528
Who do you think took it?

739
00:49:29,070 --> 00:49:30,739
It's a huge amount.

740
00:49:31,323 --> 00:49:35,076
Unless the president, facility manager,
and the accountant worked together…

741
00:49:35,160 --> 00:49:37,329
So they took it together?

742
00:49:38,246 --> 00:49:41,792
I just mean it's not certain,
but it's a possibility.

743
00:49:42,667 --> 00:49:44,211
-Zip it up.
-You little…

744
00:49:44,294 --> 00:49:46,171
Wait!

745
00:49:46,254 --> 00:49:49,966
I'm a professional in this field!
How would you get it without me?

746
00:49:53,762 --> 00:49:55,889
What do we do now, Boss?

747
00:49:56,473 --> 00:49:57,641
We need to find it.

748
00:49:57,724 --> 00:49:59,309
I need my money!

749
00:49:59,392 --> 00:50:02,437
But if they really did take it,
how would we find it?

750
00:50:02,521 --> 00:50:04,481
Well, first…

751
00:50:05,524 --> 00:50:07,943
Let's look into those three.

752
00:50:08,652 --> 00:50:09,694
All right then.

753
00:50:10,737 --> 00:50:12,447
It's going to take a while.

754
00:50:12,531 --> 00:50:15,283
Boss, you have to maintain
your position as the president

755
00:50:15,367 --> 00:50:16,701
to make the investigation easier.

756
00:50:17,619 --> 00:50:21,039
Then we'll have to continue
the intermittent family act.

757
00:50:23,625 --> 00:50:24,501
I CAN DO IT!

758
00:50:24,584 --> 00:50:26,044
Read the textbook and follow along.

759
00:50:26,670 --> 00:50:28,296
Unfair dismissal is clearly defined

760
00:50:28,380 --> 00:50:31,716
in Article 23, Paragraph 1
of the Labor Standards Act.

761
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:36,054
Simply put,
it's a dismissal without a valid reason.

762
00:50:38,306 --> 00:50:40,559
Right. This is an unfair dismissal.

763
00:50:41,309 --> 00:50:43,562
That's why I felt so angry.

764
00:50:44,312 --> 00:50:46,690
Why didn't I think
of the Labor Standards Act?

765
00:50:47,274 --> 00:50:49,234
I should've protested by citing it.

766
00:50:49,985 --> 00:50:52,696
This is all because I didn't study enough.

767
00:50:52,779 --> 00:50:54,906
I should focus on studying.

768
00:50:59,369 --> 00:51:01,246
Why am I using this right now?

769
00:51:02,289 --> 00:51:04,124
Well, kids are innocent.

770
00:51:04,207 --> 00:51:05,542
Gyeong-buk is innocent.

771
00:51:10,255 --> 00:51:12,924
I brought your things.
Let's talk for a moment.

772
00:51:13,008 --> 00:51:15,385
What? He's in front of my house right now?

773
00:51:23,727 --> 00:51:25,687
CIVIL LAW KEY POINTS

774
00:51:29,524 --> 00:51:30,650
What's going on?

775
00:51:30,734 --> 00:51:33,236
Did you change your job
to an express delivery guy?

776
00:51:41,161 --> 00:51:42,704
How have you been?

777
00:51:43,288 --> 00:51:44,831
What kind of greeting is that?

778
00:51:44,915 --> 00:51:46,041
We saw each other yesterday.

779
00:51:49,586 --> 00:51:51,504
We didn't see each other this morning.

780
00:51:58,303 --> 00:52:01,097
I came in person
because I had something to tell you.

781
00:52:02,807 --> 00:52:05,268
Good. I have something to say too.

782
00:52:05,352 --> 00:52:07,479
Article 23, Paragraph 1
of the Labor Standards Act

783
00:52:07,562 --> 00:52:09,022
states that an employer

784
00:52:09,105 --> 00:52:11,983
shall not dismiss an employee
without justifiable cause.

785
00:52:12,984 --> 00:52:14,402
What's the reason for my dismissal?

786
00:52:16,112 --> 00:52:17,447
I made a mistake.

787
00:52:17,530 --> 00:52:20,825
We still need you, Ms. Kang.

788
00:52:21,493 --> 00:52:23,244
Please come back to work.

789
00:52:23,328 --> 00:52:24,162
What?

790
00:52:25,246 --> 00:52:27,958
You fired me yesterday,
and now you want me to come back?

791
00:52:28,041 --> 00:52:29,125
I'm sorry.

792
00:52:29,209 --> 00:52:30,752
You must be quite upset.

793
00:52:30,835 --> 00:52:32,837
I promise to compensate you for--

794
00:52:32,921 --> 00:52:34,714
Excuse me, Mr. Park.

795
00:52:34,798 --> 00:52:36,091
I do like money,

796
00:52:36,174 --> 00:52:38,677
but don't try to solve everything
with your money.

797
00:52:38,760 --> 00:52:40,345
You should be apologizing

798
00:52:40,428 --> 00:52:42,722
and reflecting
for firing someone like that.

799
00:52:45,850 --> 00:52:47,852
I apologize, Ms. Kang.

800
00:52:49,396 --> 00:52:50,772
I am sincerely sorry

801
00:52:51,815 --> 00:52:54,609
if I upset you.

802
00:52:56,236 --> 00:52:57,696
Please work for two more weeks.

803
00:53:00,198 --> 00:53:03,743
It would be harsh to ignore you
when you're begging me like this.

804
00:53:04,577 --> 00:53:06,955
I'll work for two more weeks
as I promised.

805
00:53:09,207 --> 00:53:10,208
Thank you.

806
00:53:15,171 --> 00:53:16,548
Whose car is that?

807
00:53:17,132 --> 00:53:18,591
I think it's an employee's.

808
00:53:20,635 --> 00:53:23,304
Hello, everyone.

809
00:53:23,388 --> 00:53:25,056
Please, sit.

810
00:53:29,269 --> 00:53:32,188
You got all the security footage,
didn't you?

811
00:53:32,272 --> 00:53:33,273
Yes.

812
00:53:34,357 --> 00:53:35,942
Did you find anything interesting?

813
00:53:36,901 --> 00:53:40,196
Among the cars
entering and leaving Oman New Town,

814
00:53:41,281 --> 00:53:44,492
there's one car going in and out
besides the construction vehicles.

815
00:53:44,576 --> 00:53:45,952
We're looking into it now.

816
00:53:46,745 --> 00:53:48,079
Really?

817
00:53:51,458 --> 00:53:55,462
Then we'll find out who that jerk is soon.

818
00:53:58,757 --> 00:53:59,758
President Park.

819
00:54:04,220 --> 00:54:05,180
Hello, Mr. Choi.

820
00:54:05,263 --> 00:54:08,058
What brings you here so early?

821
00:54:08,141 --> 00:54:11,061
And you're here alone
without your family today.

822
00:54:12,228 --> 00:54:16,483
I couldn't sleep all night
thinking about how to run this place,

823
00:54:16,566 --> 00:54:18,151
so I just came to work early.

824
00:54:20,361 --> 00:54:23,448
You were thinking about that all night?

825
00:54:25,992 --> 00:54:26,993
Mr. Choi.

826
00:54:28,036 --> 00:54:32,665
What's the most urgent issue
in our apartment complex right now?

827
00:54:33,833 --> 00:54:36,920
Well, there's the elevator repair issue.

828
00:54:38,713 --> 00:54:40,757
-Elevator repair?
-Yes.

829
00:54:42,592 --> 00:54:44,344
How do we pay for that?

830
00:54:44,427 --> 00:54:45,845
With the reserve fund.

831
00:54:46,554 --> 00:54:48,765
-The long-term repair reserve fund?
-Yes.

832
00:54:50,183 --> 00:54:51,601
It would cost quite a lot.

833
00:54:51,684 --> 00:54:54,145
Will there be any issues using the fund?

834
00:54:55,230 --> 00:54:56,648
Not at all.

835
00:54:56,731 --> 00:54:59,567
This is exactly
what the reserve fund is for.

836
00:54:59,651 --> 00:55:03,863
But the elevator's been
breaking down quite often,

837
00:55:03,947 --> 00:55:07,283
so the repair company
agreed to fix it for free this time.

838
00:55:09,077 --> 00:55:11,204
So when we need to use the reserve fund,

839
00:55:11,287 --> 00:55:14,582
I stamp it as the president,
then you stamp it,

840
00:55:14,666 --> 00:55:17,877
and the accounting manager
processes the payment?

841
00:55:17,961 --> 00:55:20,755
Yes, that's right.
When Ha-jeong returns, I mean.

842
00:55:20,839 --> 00:55:23,716
-Ha-jeong? The accounting manager?
-Yes.

843
00:55:24,551 --> 00:55:26,678
Come to think of it, I've never met her.

844
00:55:26,761 --> 00:55:31,391
Well, Ha-jeong went on vacation
for the first time in years.

845
00:55:31,474 --> 00:55:33,518
She'll be returning soon.

846
00:55:35,687 --> 00:55:37,105
Her desk is over there.

847
00:55:38,106 --> 00:55:39,440
-I see. "Kang Ha-jeong."
-Yes.

848
00:55:39,524 --> 00:55:41,776
She's right there below me
on the organizational chart.

849
00:55:44,195 --> 00:55:46,614
ACCOUNTING MANAGER
KANG HA-JEONG

850
00:55:47,907 --> 00:55:49,409
I'd love to meet her soon.

851
00:55:53,246 --> 00:55:58,334
He skipped work
after he was just elected president.

852
00:55:58,418 --> 00:56:01,379
Did he come to work on time today?

853
00:56:02,839 --> 00:56:04,924
You cut open Gyeong-buk's piggy bank?

854
00:56:05,008 --> 00:56:07,093
Gyeong-nam, stop.

855
00:56:07,177 --> 00:56:09,470
Don't get blood on your hands.

856
00:56:10,180 --> 00:56:11,264
Just like this.

857
00:56:11,764 --> 00:56:13,975
I'll cut him open exactly the same way
and go to jail.

858
00:56:14,058 --> 00:56:15,143
-Move.
-Seriously?

859
00:56:15,226 --> 00:56:16,227
Stop it.

860
00:56:17,228 --> 00:56:19,856
To be honest, I needed some money.

861
00:56:19,939 --> 00:56:21,316
This place…

862
00:56:23,026 --> 00:56:25,987
is actually a gambling den.

863
00:56:26,070 --> 00:56:28,573
A few old folks
are playing gambling games,

864
00:56:28,656 --> 00:56:30,200
but they're terrible at them.

865
00:56:30,283 --> 00:56:32,160
I can easily earn money here.

866
00:56:33,286 --> 00:56:35,205
Shut that mouth.

867
00:56:35,288 --> 00:56:37,790
Hey, stop. Someone might see.

868
00:56:40,627 --> 00:56:43,379
Right, Father. So…

869
00:56:44,339 --> 00:56:46,466
Were you trying to gamble again?

870
00:56:47,342 --> 00:56:49,552
Do you want your hands cut off?

871
00:56:51,429 --> 00:56:52,639
Go home.

872
00:57:08,613 --> 00:57:09,614
My gosh.

873
00:57:10,240 --> 00:57:12,325
Those jerks.

874
00:57:13,493 --> 00:57:16,454
How could they threaten their dad,
even if he has a gambling problem?

875
00:57:18,456 --> 00:57:20,124
That is unforgivable, seriously.

876
00:57:21,251 --> 00:57:22,293
Mom!

877
00:57:23,836 --> 00:57:25,046
Here. Take this.

878
00:57:27,215 --> 00:57:28,675
I just found it.

879
00:57:29,425 --> 00:57:31,886
My dad told me
I shouldn't eat stuff lying around.

880
00:57:31,970 --> 00:57:34,514
Hey, don't you get what I mean?

881
00:57:35,431 --> 00:57:37,058
I like you.

882
00:57:38,059 --> 00:57:39,894
I only like my mom, Kang Ha-ri.

883
00:57:43,439 --> 00:57:44,440
Bye, Gyeong-buk.

884
00:57:44,524 --> 00:57:46,651
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

885
00:57:48,278 --> 00:57:49,445
-I don't know.
-Did you fight?

886
00:57:50,029 --> 00:57:51,864
-What?
-Why do you look so upset?

887
00:57:54,117 --> 00:57:56,286
-Did you eat a lot for lunch?
-Mom!

888
00:57:57,954 --> 00:58:00,081
Mom!

889
00:58:04,252 --> 00:58:07,255
So Hye-jun said she liked you,
but you rejected her?

890
00:58:08,798 --> 00:58:10,508
Why? Is she not pretty?

891
00:58:11,092 --> 00:58:13,177
I like you the most, Mom.

892
00:58:13,761 --> 00:58:15,305
You're the prettiest.

893
00:58:15,888 --> 00:58:17,473
Oh my gosh.

894
00:58:17,557 --> 00:58:20,393
You're so silly.

895
00:58:20,476 --> 00:58:21,936
But Gyeong-buk,

896
00:58:22,020 --> 00:58:24,606
I really can't get used to this.

897
00:58:24,689 --> 00:58:27,650
Can't you just call me Ha-ri
when no one's around?

898
00:58:27,734 --> 00:58:30,737
It's so awkward when you call me Mom.

899
00:58:30,820 --> 00:58:33,323
-Can you do that for me?
-Okay, Ha-ri.

900
00:58:34,073 --> 00:58:35,199
I'll buy you chocolate milk.

901
00:58:35,283 --> 00:58:37,201
-Yes!
-Yes!

902
00:58:44,167 --> 00:58:46,294
What the heck did I just hear?

903
00:58:47,086 --> 00:58:48,087
"Ha-ri"?

904
00:58:48,921 --> 00:58:50,256
He called her by her first name?

905
00:58:53,343 --> 00:58:55,094
It's so sweet, Mom.

906
00:58:55,178 --> 00:58:56,179
"Ha-ri."

907
00:58:57,055 --> 00:58:58,389
It's so sweet, Ha-ri.

908
00:59:01,267 --> 00:59:02,518
It's tasty, right?

909
00:59:05,730 --> 00:59:06,731
Ha-ri.

910
00:59:06,814 --> 00:59:09,317
Ha-jeong, what are you doing here?

911
00:59:09,901 --> 00:59:11,069
What about you?

912
00:59:12,028 --> 00:59:13,613
Who is that, Mom?

913
00:59:16,324 --> 00:59:17,492
"Mom"?

914
00:59:23,665 --> 00:59:25,667
Well, it's…

915
00:59:36,969 --> 00:59:39,222
It's so strange.

916
00:59:39,305 --> 00:59:41,933
Do you want your hands cut off?

917
00:59:42,850 --> 00:59:46,229
The way those jerks spoke to their father…

918
00:59:46,813 --> 00:59:49,315
Can't you just call me Ha-ri
when no one's around?

919
00:59:49,399 --> 00:59:52,151
And she told him to call her
by her first name.

920
00:59:55,822 --> 00:59:58,449
Whatever. Forget it.

921
00:59:58,533 --> 00:59:59,867
It's not my business.

922
01:00:02,078 --> 01:00:02,912
Right.

923
01:00:03,913 --> 01:00:06,999
What family doesn't have problems?

924
01:00:09,293 --> 01:00:11,254
Right. Every family does.

925
01:00:17,176 --> 01:00:18,511
But still…

926
01:00:19,262 --> 01:00:21,889
It's the president's family.

927
01:00:21,973 --> 01:00:25,184
The president's family
shouldn't have issues like that.

928
01:00:28,980 --> 01:00:33,276
-Dad, the elevator's broken.
-It's broken?

929
01:00:33,860 --> 01:00:36,195
Mr. Park, let me talk to you for a second.

930
01:00:47,957 --> 01:00:49,167
What is it?

931
01:00:49,250 --> 01:00:51,753
We looked into the owner of that car, sir.

932
01:00:53,796 --> 01:00:55,965
What? It's Park Hae-kang.

933
01:00:56,048 --> 01:00:58,050
It's the only one
besides the construction vehicles

934
01:00:58,134 --> 01:01:01,137
and the cars whose owners
we've identified.

935
01:01:07,852 --> 01:01:09,020
Then does that mean

936
01:01:09,103 --> 01:01:12,774
Park Hae-kang planted them
to raise housing prices

937
01:01:12,857 --> 01:01:15,026
and get elected as the president?

938
01:01:15,109 --> 01:01:17,320
Yes, it seems so.

939
01:01:20,323 --> 01:01:21,616
Wow.

940
01:01:22,950 --> 01:01:24,619
President Park Hae-kang…

941
01:01:26,120 --> 01:01:28,289
He's quite something.

942
01:01:30,458 --> 01:01:33,294
Mr. Park, I'm sorry,
but I can't work here anymore.

943
01:01:33,377 --> 01:01:34,962
What do you mean?

944
01:01:36,172 --> 01:01:37,673
Something came up.

945
01:01:37,757 --> 01:01:39,550
You can't just quit like this.

946
01:01:39,634 --> 01:01:41,761
You fired me suddenly too.

947
01:01:41,844 --> 01:01:43,888
So just consider us even now.

948
01:01:43,971 --> 01:01:46,849
You already received your payment.
You should do your job.

949
01:01:46,933 --> 01:01:49,268
You said you're a professional.

950
01:01:49,352 --> 01:01:52,104
Even a professional
can have an emergency sometimes!

951
01:01:53,940 --> 01:01:56,067
What is that emergency? Let me hear it.

952
01:01:57,527 --> 01:01:58,444
I can't tell you.

953
01:01:58,528 --> 01:02:00,947
What's the point in being your wife
for two more weeks?

954
01:02:01,030 --> 01:02:04,492
You already got the position
that you wanted so badly.

955
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:08,579
Our family still needs you, Ms. Kang.

956
01:02:08,663 --> 01:02:12,458
Mr. Park, that family you speak of
is fake anyway!

957
01:02:13,709 --> 01:02:14,961
What?

958
01:02:15,044 --> 01:02:16,254
"Fake"?

959
01:02:16,337 --> 01:02:18,214
Oh my goodness. You…

960
01:02:19,799 --> 01:02:21,968
So you guys

961
01:02:22,760 --> 01:02:24,262
were a fake family?

962
01:02:28,766 --> 01:02:31,477
THE APARTMENT JOB

963
01:02:55,585 --> 01:02:57,503
Emptying out the entire account
makes no sense.

964
01:02:57,587 --> 01:03:00,131
Make something that requires you
to use the fund.

965
01:03:00,214 --> 01:03:01,966
-Let's find…
-Defects!

966
01:03:02,633 --> 01:03:05,344
Since it's an emergency,
I'll allow a wide range of touching.

967
01:03:05,428 --> 01:03:07,054
I can tell that you're faking it.

968
01:03:07,138 --> 01:03:08,180
-Ms. Jang!
-Ms. Jang!

969
01:03:08,264 --> 01:03:11,392
He would've found out
that the account is empty.

970
01:03:13,019 --> 01:03:16,647
The reserve fund. He became the president
to pocket the fund.

971
01:03:16,731 --> 01:03:17,565
We don't have time.

972
01:03:17,648 --> 01:03:19,984
Find anything that can be paid for
out of the reserve fund.

973
01:03:21,193 --> 01:03:23,529
Precisely 123 households
have a heating bill of zero.

974
01:03:23,613 --> 01:03:24,864
President Park.

975
01:03:24,947 --> 01:03:27,617
Then will you become
another Heating Bill Martyr?

976
01:03:27,700 --> 01:03:29,368
Heating Bill Martyr…

977
01:03:29,452 --> 01:03:30,786
I don't get how Park found out.

978
01:03:30,870 --> 01:03:32,079
I won't let it happen again--

979
01:03:32,163 --> 01:03:33,205
I'm enjoying this,

980
01:03:33,289 --> 01:03:35,333
so just let Park Hae-kang
do what he wants.

981
01:03:38,836 --> 01:03:40,838
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

